   "text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nLRU Cache with Time-To-Live (TTL) Expiry\n\nThis module provides a thread-safe LRU cache implementation that supports\nexpiration of entries after a configurable time-to-live period.\n\nFeatures:\n    - Least Recently Used (LRU) eviction policy\n    - Per-key TTL (time-to-live) expiry\n    - Thread-safe operations via a reentrant lock\n    - Clean, well-documented Python module\n\nDesign:\n    The cache stores items in an internal OrderedDict where the key order\n    reflects insertion/access order. On access, the item is moved to the\n    front (most recently used). When an item is added or accessed and its\n    TTL has not yet expired, it is inserted. If the cache reaches its size\n    limit, the oldest (least recently used) item is evicted.\n\nThe public API is exposed through a class ``TTLCache``. A thread-safe\nwrapper ``ThreadSafeTTLCache`` wraps the core cache and ensures that all\noperations are executed atomically across threads.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport threading\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Generic, List",
